  <p><em>Impact-specific reading of timing dynamics — drafted via the <code>market-researcher:sector-overview</code> skill against the INGO impact-fund cohort:</em></p>

  <p>The 2015–2019 vintage band is the most populated, reflecting the wave of INGO-sponsored fund formation following the SDG launch and the maturation of impact-investing as an asset class. First-time GPs today face a different attention dynamic than that wave: the post-SDG LP allocation pulse has crested, climate-finance has become the new attention magnet, and the average DFI's appetite for first-time managers is more cautious than it was in 2017–2018. The "right time" to raise depends on which LP class you're targeting: DFI anchors operate on annual fiscal cycles tied to investment-committee approval calendars (commit early in the LP's fiscal year for the highest probability of approval); foundation anchors operate on 5-year program cycles tied to strategic plans (find the foundation in the early years of a strategy refresh, not the late years); family offices vary widely but are most receptive in the first year of a new principal's interest in a thematic area.</p>

  <h2>Who anchors INGO-sponsored funds?</h2>
  <p>{{ peer_benchmarks.coverage[5].n }} of {{ peer_benchmarks.total }} funds publicly name a single anchor LP at announce or first close. Browse the <a href="{{ '/peer-funds/' | url }}">peer funds catalog</a> for which funds are which — and the LP-side catalogs (<a href="{{ '/dfis/' | url }}">DFIs</a>, <a href="{{ '/foundations/' | url }}">foundations</a>, <a href="{{ '/family-offices/' | url }}">family offices</a>) for the LP-by-LP commitment patterns.</p>

  <p><em>Impact-specific anchor-LP dynamics — drafted via the <code>market-researcher:sector-overview</code> skill against the INGO impact-fund cohort:</em></p>

  <p>Anchor type matters more than anchor count: it predicts the rest of the LP stack. A DFI anchor pulls in more DFIs — DFIs co-fund and follow each other, partly through formal co-investment platforms (FMO/BII/IFC syndications) and partly through informal information flow at conferences and committees. A foundation anchor pulls in other foundations and family offices, because foundation boards explicitly reference each other's commitments as social proof. A commercial-impact-asset-manager anchor (BlueOrchard, responsAbility, etc.) pulls institutional impact LPs and asset-management funds-of-funds. Mixed anchors at first close are usually difficult to construct and difficult to manage — most successful first closes have a clear anchor type that defines the overall LP profile. The implication for a first-time INGO-transitioning GP: pick the anchor type before the named LP, then go after the LP.</p>

